{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888569,"nonce":"jqQ6d6WXGTdhwDvfMCO2nvpbDuc=","title":"An Incident is not a notification subject, so no policy can send \"Incident #N was drawn\" anywhere","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0052 §5: declaring is a notification. `policies_subjkinds_ck` admits only `alert`, `case`, `digest` (`db/migrations/00072_a_policy_binds_a_subject_and_counts_it.sql:170`) and `notifications_subjkind_ck` has no `incident`.\n\n**The demonstration.** Creating a policy with `subject_kinds = ['incident']` is refused by the CHECK.\n\n**Why it matters.** \"Every Incident goes to incident.io\" is meant to be one catch-all policy; without the subject it cannot be written, and retries, idempotency, delivery audit and drills don't apply to Incidents.\n\n**Where.** `policies_subjkinds_ck` and `notifications_subjkind_ck` plus their Go and contract copies (the 00072 header names the literal copies that move together); the reasons an Incident emits — drawn, member added, member removed, quiet, active again; the `oto.notification.v1` envelope gains an `incident` subject carrying members (labels, deep links), the drawing Correlator or actor, active/quiet, and a deep link; delivered over the generic webhook channel. `threads_subjkind_ck` is **not** touched here — an Incident becomes a conversation only when a Correlator makes its Incidents conversations, which is its own ticket.\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** A policy bound to `incident` routes Incident facts to a webhook channel; each fact is one idempotent Notification; the envelope carries the metadata above; no reason value means resolve or close; an org with no such policy sends nothing; golden tests pin the envelope; `threads_subjkind_ck` is unchanged.\n\n**Blocked by.** `b2672a1`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}